13:37:19.231  === HOW THE BYTES LEAVE ===
13:37:19.231  One address (0x80), four variants, about a minute. Ignition in position 2 or the
13:37:19.232  engine running - the modules are asleep otherwise and nothing can answer.

13:37:19.232  Setup already matches the vendor byte for byte. The untested difference is that it
13:37:19.233  writes one byte at a time with gaps, and we write whole frames at once.

13:37:19.880    idle check: receive line high in 100% of 200 samples  (steady high - what a powered K-line should look like)

